       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there is a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg intended.\n\nAlso, medication orders normally need to come from a licensed prescriber. I can't verify that this one has been authorized.\n\n- **If a prescriber intended a standard dose**, tell me the intended dose. Typical adult dosing is 25\u201350 mg daily to start, up to 200 mg daily. I can enter the order once the prescriber confirms it.\n- **If 1000 mg was truly intended**, it needs to go through the prescriber and pharmacy for verification. I wouldn't enter it as written.\n\nWhich dose should I enter, and who is the prescribing clinician?"
